<section class="game-guide post-body">
<h2>How to play free baccarat</h2>
<p>Pick a chip, bet on <b>Player</b>, <b>Banker</b> or <b>Tie</b>, and press <b>Deal</b>. Two hands are dealt and the one closer to 9 wins. You never make a decision after the bet: every draw follows a fixed rule.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Aces count 1, tens and face cards count 0, and only the last digit of a total matters. A 7 and an 8 make 5.</li>
  <li>An 8 or 9 on the first two cards is a natural and ends the hand.</li>
  <li>Otherwise the Player hand draws on 0 through 5, and the Banker draws by a set table that depends on the Player's third card. The log explains each draw in plain English.</li>
  <li>Player pays {{ baccaratOdds.payoutStr.player }}. Banker pays {{ baccaratOdds.payoutStr.banker }} minus a {{ baccaratOdds.bankerCommissionPct }}% commission. Tie pays {{ baccaratOdds.payoutStr.tie }}, and Player and Banker bets push on a tie.</li>
</ul>
<p>For the full rules see <a href="/strategy/baccarat/how-to-play/">how to play baccarat</a>, or compare the three bets in <a href="/strategy/baccarat/banker-vs-player-vs-tie/">Banker vs Player vs Tie</a>.</p>

